potsherd's engine (`packages/core`) is a hard fork of episodic-memory. The
upstream revision the fork was taken from is:

  upstream: obra/episodic-memory
  tag:      v1.4.2
  commit:   10757690210574421f1df5f35835af8d0c74d984
  date:     2026-05-21

That revision is reachable from this repository as the fetch-only git remote
`upstream-episodic`, so `git log upstream-episodic/main` and
`git diff 1075769..upstream-episodic/main -- src/` keep working:

  git remote add upstream-episodic https://github.com/obra/episodic-memory.git
  git fetch upstream-episodic --no-tags \
    'refs/heads/main:refs/remotes/upstream-episodic/main'

No upstream commit is merged into this history. Files were hand-ported into
potsherd's layer layout and each one carries a provenance header naming the
upstream path and revision. `docs/upstream/PORT-LOG.md` lists every upstream
source file and records whether it was taken verbatim, adapted, or refused,
and why.

The secret-detection rule pack in `packages/core/src/redact-rules.ts` (L2,
`plans/03-ARCHITECTURE.md` §5) is ported from gitleaks' `config/gitleaks.toml`
and from secretlint's `@secretlint/secretlint-rule-preset-recommend`. Neither
project's runtime is a dependency: the patterns were transcribed and each rule
records its upstream rule id in its `source` field. No rule in that file was
written from memory.

Generic fixes made here are prepared as upstream pull requests under
`docs/upstream/` and are not submitted by any agent.

Third-party dependencies retain their own licenses; see the `licenses`
section of each package's `package.json` and `node_modules`.

History rewrite, 22 August 2026
-------------------------------
`docs/upstream/PHASE-1-SCOUT.md` published real transcript prose — an assistant
`thinking` block and a truncated `<user_query>`, both from one machine's private
sessions — from phase 1 until 22 August 2026. The samples are synthetic now, and
that path was removed from every commit with `git filter-repo` and force-pushed,
so the leaked blob is not reachable from any commit on `origin/main`.

The root commit after the rewrite is `6697ca9`, and the `v1.0.0` tag now points at
`548b5b5`, whose tree no longer contains the file.
**A clone taken before 22 August 2026 still holds the original blob.** Re-clone
rather than pull if you have one.
